icitly clear focus or dismiss the keyboard before navigating to the songs list page, so returning to the index page doesn't bring the keyboard back up and block clicks on the mini player.\n\nChecking the math, the keyboard's screen coverage does overlap where the bottom mini player sits, so this is a real risk unless the page avoids resizing around the focused input. I should also note the SongSheet closes after clicking play, with the sheet height taking up 70% of the screen.\n\nOne more ambiguity: on SongsListPage the mini player needs to be laid out alongside the list using layoutWeight so it doesn't overlap list items, and the spinner state shouldn't hide the mini player. There's also a selector collision risk — if a song title matches the search keyword, the TextInput's text attribute would equal the song title too, making BY.text() ambiguous between the input and the list/mini player.\n\nI also need artist strings to be consistent everywhere (list, sheet, mini player, play page) since the same song must display identically across views, and the play page's pause state in the mini player is likely only reflected via icon image rather than text, which could be hard for a test to detect through text-based selectors.\n\nI should avoid adding visible \"播放\"/\"暂停\"","startTime":1792338800499,"lastModifiedTime":1792338822755},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01Fxn7JJPsmgqfqZGKmuoMSx","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"cd /Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec102 && export PATH=/Applications/DevEco-Studio.app/Contents/sdk/default/openharmony/toolchains:$PATH && D=127.0.0.1:5555 && hdc -t $D shell \"uitest dumpLayout -p /data/local/tmp/b11.json\" >/dev/null; hdc -t $D file recv /data/local/tmp/b11.json logs/baseline/b11-before-restart.json >/dev/null; hdc -t $D shell \"aa force-stop cc.chenlvin.cloudmusic\"; hdc -t $D shell \"aa start -a EntryAbility -b cc.chenlvin.cloudmusic\"; sleep 4; hdc -t $D shell \"uitest dumpLayout -p /data/local/tmp/b12