lence to the down arrow, and play/pause state syncing between the playback page and mini-player in both directions.\n\nI'm also noting that the mini-player itself should have its own play/pause button, though this isn't confirmed by the source material, and I'm starting to build out S2 items covering the homepage search results list and tapping into it.\n\nNow I'm working through S2's remaining assertions: tapping a song opens an action panel, tapping \"Play\" closes the panel and triggers a request for the play URL, successful playback updates the mini-player with the song title, artist, and playing state, switching songs resets the mini-player and progress to zero, and failed playback leaves the mini-player unchanged. Moving into S3, I'm covering navigation back to the homepage, the mini-player persisting the same song info, playback continuing uninterrupted across that navigation, and tapping the mini-player's non-button area to re-enter the playback page.\n\nThen I start S4: the mini-player shows elapsed time in m:ss format starting at \"0:00\" and increments as playback continues, the playback page includes a draggable slider showing current time and total duration, dragging or tapping the slider seeks the player and updates the displayed current time to the new position, progress continues advancing during playback, and collapsing the player afterward keeps the mini-player's time synced to the seeked position rather than reverting to an old value or zero.\n\nI also note some unconfirmed assumptions worth flagging: dragging the slider while paused, whether the mini-player persists after app restart, whether it hides after playback ends, consistency between the top-right playback popup and the mini-player/playback page states, whether the mini-player appears at the bottom of playlist pages, and anti-duplicate behavior where repeated taps on the cover or mini-player only open one playback page, and repeated taps on the down arrow only navigate back once.\n\n","st