esult was actually served from cache rather than a live network response.\n\nBut the hilog data shows a fresh timestamp consistent with the actual request time, meaning it really did reach a live server, so the emulator must be able to connect to 192.168.1.97:3000 even though the host can't. Since there's no curl on the device, I should check whether toybox has wget or nc available, or try verifying connectivity some other way before touching app state.\n\n","startTime":1792374491984,"lastModifiedTime":1792374495221},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_018Q4GEhtvwVy5DT2DEwDcyt","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"export PATH=/Applications/DevEco-Studio.app/Contents/sdk/default/openharmony/toolchains:$PATH && D=127.0.0.1:5555 && hdc -t $D shell \"ping -c 1 -W 2 192.168.1.97 2>&1 | head -3; ping -c 1 -W 2 172.24.16.249 2>&1 | head -3; ls /system/bin | grep -E -w 'nc|netcat|wget|curl|toybox|busybox'\"; ifconfig | grep -E \"inet \" ; route -n get 192.168.1.97 2>/dev/null | grep -E \"interface|gateway\"","description":"Test emulator reachability of candidate host IPs","prefix_rule":"[\"hdc\",\"-t\"]"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\nPing 192.168.1.97 (192.168.1.97): 56(84) bytes.\n\n--- 192.168.1.97 ping statistics ---\nPing 172.24.16.249 (172.24.16.249): 56(84) bytes.\n64 bytes from 172.24.16.249: icmp_seq=0 ttl=255 time=8456 ms\n\ntoybox\n\tinet 127.0.0.1 netmask 0xff000000\n\tinet 172.24.16.249 netmask 0xfffffc00 broadcast 172.24.19.255\n    gateway: 172.24.16.1\n  interface: en0\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec102","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"yolo","taskId":"p4iwfk","output":"Ping 192.168.1.97 (192.168.1.97): 56(84) bytes.\n\n--- 192.168.1.97 ping statistics ---\nPing 172.24.16.249 (172.24.16.249): 56(84) bytes.\n64 bytes from 172.24.16.249: icmp_seq=0 ttl=255 time=8456 ms\n\ntoybox\n\tinet 127.0.0.1 netmask 0xff000000\n\tinet 172.24.16.